[center][color=#f59e0b][size=6][b]R O M A N T A S Y[/b][/size][/color]
[color=#b8a285][size=3]Your adventures, remembered. Your bond, earned.[/size][/color]
[color=#b8a285]A relationship framework for Skyrim SE/AE[/color]
[color=#d99563][b]Version 4.0.0 • The Rosewater ledger, hosted by Magelight UI[/b][/color]

[color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]What's New in 3.0[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]The Rosewater ledger[/color] - Romantasy's ledger and pop-ups are now a page hosted by Magelight UI. [b]Meridian UI, Prisma UI and Media Keys Fix are not needed.[/b] It keeps the familiar full-screen ledger, dossiers and settings.[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]New Bond, rebuilt[/color] - give any eligible follower their own likes and dislikes from a full-screen page, with a searchable list of every deed. Their personality is saved as a small profile file, and you can edit, reset or remove the bond at any time.[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Your 2.x bonds come with you[/color] - player-created bonds from earlier versions migrate automatically, keeping their likes, dislikes and points.[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Full controller support[/color] - navigate everything with a gamepad, with on-screen button hints. Open the dashboard with the Romantasy power from your Favorites.[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Any language[/color] - names in Russian, Greek, Chinese, Japanese, Korean, Polish, Czech and other languages display correctly, and are capitalised in titles just like English names. [i](3.0.1)[/i][/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Clear feedback[/color] - a short message confirms when a bond is added, edited, reset or removed.[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Simple profiles for follower authors[/color] - support a follower with one small text file. No romance factions, scripts, globals or Romantasy master are needed, and dialogue can read the bond directly.[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Nothing breaks[/color] - existing follower integrations, dialogue conditions and the Papyrus API keep working as before.[/*]
[/list]


[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]Author's Note[/color][/b][/size]

I wanted romance in Skyrim to grow out of the way you actually play, not out of a menu. Romantasy watches the adventure you are already having and quietly turns it into a bond, one dungeon, one quest, one bad decision at a time. It does not replace your follower mods and it does not write anyone's personality. It only keeps the ledger.

Followers can arrive with a personality written by their author, or you can create one yourself for any follower who does not have one, right from the dashboard. Either way, the adventure is what moves the relationship.

If you are a mod author and you build something on top of it, please tell me. I would genuinely love to play it.


[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]Overview[/color][/b][/size]

[b][color=#fbbf24]A standalone, save-safe relationship system that turns the way you play into a deepening bond with each of your followers.[/color][/b]
Six tiers, one built-in dashboard, zero micromanagement.

Romantasy tracks your actions across [color=#fbbf24]58 categories of play[/color] (combat, exploration, crafting, crime, guild work, vampire and werewolf life, and more) and converts them into relationship points for every follower it manages. Each follower has individual likes and dislikes. Doing what she loves raises the bond. Doing what she hates wounds it.

The bond climbs through six tiers: [color=#fbbf24]Stranger[/color], [color=#fbbf24]Acquaintance[/color], [color=#fbbf24]Friend[/color], [color=#fbbf24]Confidant[/color], [color=#fbbf24]Lover[/color], and finally [color=#fbbf24]Spouse[/color]. Follower mods can hang dialogue, scenes, voiced reactions, quest beats, or marriage hooks off any of them.

Romantasy slots underneath your existing follower mods without taking them over. It does not replace the vanilla follower system, Horde, NFF, AFT, EFF, custom follower controllers, or the vanilla marriage system. It is the scoreboard; the follower's author is still the writer.

[color=#b8a285][b]Release note:[/b] the plugin is ESL-flagged, the SKSE DLL is digitally signed, earned points save and restore with your save game, and personalities are kept in small profile files you can back up.[/color]


[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]Features[/color][/b][/size]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]The Ledger[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]58 tracked activities[/color] - dungeons cleared, quests and questlines finished, locks picked, necks bitten, potions mixed, murders committed, and much more[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Weighted points[/color] - finishing a guild questline moves the bond far more than picking one pocket; every activity has its own weight[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Individual personalities[/color] - author-supplied and player-created followers can each like, dislike, or ignore every activity[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Shared adventure only[/color] - automatic activity points are awarded or removed only while that follower is actively following you; someone waiting at home does not react[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Independent bonds[/color] - spawned or duplicated followers that share the same base NPC share one personality but keep separate names and point totals[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Event-driven tracking[/color] - the plugin reacts to the game's own statistic events in native code; there are no Papyrus polling loops[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Save-safe persistence[/color] - earned points and recent changes are stored in each save's SKSE co-save, so every save keeps its own story[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]The Dashboard[/color][/b][/size]

The dashboard is a page hosted by Magelight UI, which must be installed.

[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Your Company[/color] - see every bond with current points, tier, role, progress, and following or away status[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Follower dossiers[/color] - open any follower to see likes, dislikes, milestones, and the five most recent point changes[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]New Bond[/color] - a full-screen page for adding a follower who is travelling with you and has no author support. Choose the companion, then stamp each deed Like, Neutral or Dislike. Deeds are grouped into seven categories, a search box finds any deed as you type, and a live preview shows the personality before you seal it.[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Protected author profiles[/color] - personalities supplied by follower authors are sealed and clearly identified; players and other integrations cannot overwrite them[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Editable player profiles[/color] - Edit personality, Reset bond, or Remove bond for any bond you created yourself; reset and remove ask for confirmation first[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Confirmation messages[/color] - a short notice tells you when a bond was added, edited, reset or removed, or why it could not be[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Away-follower control[/color] - choose whether companions who are not currently following remain visible in the ledger[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Milestone tracker[/color] - always know how far the current bond is from the next tier[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Resolution independent[/color] - the interface scales proportionally across resolutions and aspect ratios, including ultrawide[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Controller Support[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Full navigation[/color] - the D-pad moves between every row, button, setting and deed stamp; A selects; B goes back or closes[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Scrolling[/color] - the left stick scrolls the company list, dossiers and preference lists[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Button hints[/color] - on-screen hints appear when you pick up the controller and hide when you return to keyboard and mouse[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Opening[/color] - turn on Open with Favorites Menu in Settings, then cast the Romantasy power from your Favorites[/*]
[/list]

[color=#b8a285]The LB + X opening shortcut from 2.x has been removed; use the Favorites power instead. Typing, such as searching deeds, needs a keyboard.[/color]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Notifications[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Tier pop-ups[/color] - a short ceremonial pop-up appears when a bond crosses into a new tier, up or down, showing how many points the moment was worth[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Two moods, two scores[/color] - deepened bonds get a warm fanfare, wounded bonds get a somber piece; each plays with a gentle fade[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Combat aware[/color] - tier notifications are held until the fight ends, so the moment is never buried mid-battle[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Unobtrusive[/color] - pop-ups do not pause the game, close themselves after 20 seconds, and close instantly with Enter, A or B; gain and loss pop-ups can each be switched off in Settings[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Two Ways to Open[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Hotkey mode[/color] - Left Ctrl + R toggles the dashboard (default)[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Favorites mode[/color] - enable one setting and Romantasy grants you a favorited lesser power that opens the dashboard when cast; ideal for controller players. This replaces the hotkey until you switch it off.[/*]
[/list]


[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]The Six Tiers[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Stranger[/color] - 0 points[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Acquaintance[/color] - 500 points[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Friend[/color] - 1,000 points[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Confidant[/color] - 1,500 points[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Lover[/color] - 2,000 points[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Spouse[/color] - 2,500 points[/*]
[/list]

Bonds can fall as well as rise. A follower who watches you do the things she hates will drift back down through the tiers, and the dashboard will show you the damage.

[color=#b8a285][b]Important:[/b] Spouse is a Romantasy relationship tier. It does not automatically perform Skyrim's vanilla marriage ceremony, and adding a bond does not give a follower new voiced dialogue.[/color]


[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Skyrim Special Edition 1.5.97 or a supported Anniversary Edition runtime[/*]
[*][url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE64[/url] matching your Skyrim runtime[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/url] matching your Skyrim runtime[/*]
[*]Magelight UI 1.6 or newer[/*]
[/list]

[color=#b8a285]That is all. Romantasy does not require Meridian UI, Prisma UI or Media Keys Fix, and needs no SkyUI or MCM. Skyrim VR is not supported by the dashboard.[/color]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]Installation[/color][/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install SKSE64, Address Library and Magelight UI with your mod manager.[/*]
[*]Install Romantasy with your mod manager (MO2, Vortex, etc.). Keep the bundled page files, scripts, sounds and licenses.[/*]
[*]Activate [font=Courier New]CS_Romantasy.esp[/font] in your load order.[/*]
[*]If a follower offers Romantasy support as a separate download, install it alongside the follower.[/*]
[*]Launch the game and go adventuring.[/*]
[/list]

There is no MCM, no INI to edit, and no quest for the player to start.

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]Upgrading from 2.x[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Install 4.0.0 over your previous version. Your saves keep their points.[/*]
[*]Romantasy no longer needs Meridian UI. Keep Meridian only if another mod you use requires it.[/*]
[*]Bonds you created yourself in 2.x migrate automatically the first time each follower is loaded, keeping likes, dislikes and points.[/*]
[*]If you opened Romantasy with LB + X, switch on Open with Favorites Menu in Settings and use the Romantasy power instead.[/*]
[/list]

[color=#b8a285][b]Existing saves:[/b] Romantasy can be added mid-playthrough. A new bond begins at 0 unless the follower author supplies a different starting tier. Romantasy cannot reconstruct adventures that happened before it was installed.[/color]


[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]How to Use[/color][/b][/size]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Controls[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Left Ctrl + R[/color] - open or close the dashboard in hotkey mode[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Romantasy power[/color] - in Favorites mode, cast the granted lesser power to open the dashboard[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Esc or B[/color] - close a confirmation, leave the New Bond page, or close the dashboard[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Mouse, keyboard or controller[/color] - all three work everywhere in the dashboard[/*]
[/list]

The dashboard pauses the game while it is open. Tier pop-ups do not.

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Author-Supported Followers[/color][/b][/size]

Followers with author support appear automatically. Their personality card is marked [color=#fbbf24]Author-defined personality[/color] and is read-only. The follower author controls those likes and dislikes, along with any dialogue, reactions, scenes, or romance pacing connected to the bond.

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Creating a New Bond[/color][/b][/size]

Bring a follower without author support along with you, open the dashboard and choose [color=#fbbf24]New bond[/color]. Pick the companion, stamp the deeds she likes and dislikes, and choose [color=#fbbf24]Begin bond[/color].

[list]
[*]The personality is saved to [font=Courier New]SKSE/Plugins/Romantasy/PlayerProfiles[/font] and applies immediately. Under MO2, new profile files normally appear in Overwrite.[/*]
[*]Personalities are shared by every save that uses those files. Earned points stay separate in each save.[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Edit personality[/color] changes likes and dislikes at any time.[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Reset bond[/color] returns the selected follower to 0 points in the current save.[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Remove bond[/color] takes the follower out of the ledger for every save that uses your profiles. You can add her again later with New bond.[/*]
[/list]

[color=#b8a285]Keep the PlayerProfiles folder when you update Romantasy. Followers created at runtime by other mods, without a stable plugin record, cannot be added.[/color]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Settings[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Open with Favorites Menu (switch between hotkey and Favorites-power opening)[/*]
[*]"Romance Deepened" pop-ups on or off[/*]
[*]"Romance Wounded" pop-ups on or off[/*]
[*]Show or hide away companions in the company list[/*]
[*]Password-protected developer tools for controlled point and deed testing on actively following companions[/*]
[/list]

[color=#b8a285]Settings are saved to [font=Courier New]Data/SKSE/Plugins/Romantasy/settings.json[/font] and apply across saves.[/color]


[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]How It Works[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#fbbf24][b]Watching the adventure[/b][/color] - Romantasy listens to the same statistics screen the vanilla game already keeps. Clear a dungeon, finish a quest, pick a pocket, read a skill book: when the game records it, Romantasy asks each active follower whether she cares. If she likes it, she awards points. If she hates it, she takes some away. If she has no opinion, nothing happens.

[color=#fbbf24][b]Personalities and points[/b][/color] - a follower's personality lives in a small profile file, either supplied by her author or written by you through New bond. Her earned points live in your save. Change a personality and every save that uses it follows; play a different save and its points are its own.

[color=#fbbf24][b]Profile ownership[/b][/color] - personalities supplied by follower authors are authoritative and sealed. Player-created personalities belong to the player and can be edited or removed. Older integrations keep their own protection, so one system never silently overwrites another.

[color=#fbbf24][b]Dialogue bridge[/b][/color] - follower dialogue can check whether a follower is managed, her current tier, and her exact points with a standard Creation Kit condition. Older faction-based conditions keep working.

[color=#fbbf24][b]Per-reference identity[/b][/color] - dynamic followers are tracked by their actor reference, not only their base NPC. Multiple followers created from the same base keep separate point totals, and player-assigned display names appear correctly in the dashboard.

[color=#fbbf24][b]Persistence[/b][/color] - points and recent changes are stored in the SKSE co-save using standard serialization. Removing Romantasy forgets its own relationship ledger without taking over or rewriting the follower's original systems.


[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]For Mod Authors[/color][/b][/size]

Romantasy is a modding resource. You remain in full control of your follower's dialogue, scenes, personality, pacing, and marriage content. Romantasy supplies the centralized ledger, relationship tiers, exact point queries, notifications, dashboard, and event bridge.

[b][color=#fbbf24]New in 3.0: support a follower with a single profile file. Your follower plugin does not need Romantasy as a master, and needs no romance factions, scripts or globals.[/color][/b] Players without Romantasy keep your follower exactly as it is.

The download includes guides for profiles, follower conversion, dialogue conditions and the Papyrus API, plus an example profile and a profile checker.

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Path 1: A Profile File (recommended)[/color][/b][/size]

Ship one TOML file per follower in [font=Courier New]SKSE/Plugins/Romantasy/Profiles/[/font]:

[code]schema_version = 1

[npc]
plugin = "ExampleFollower.esp"
form_id = "0x000800"

[romance]
starting_level = "Stranger"
likes = ["Quests Completed", "Dungeons Cleared"]
dislikes = ["Murders"][/code]

[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]plugin[/color] is the plugin that defines the follower's NPC record[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]form_id[/color] is that NPC base record's plugin-local ID (for example 05000800 becomes 0x000800; an ESL's local ID is at most 0xFFF), not the placed reference[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]starting_level[/color] is Stranger through Spouse and defaults to Stranger; a save's existing points always take precedence[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]likes and dislikes[/color] accept the statistic labels or their [font=Courier New]ROM_*[/font] identifiers from the list below[/*]
[*]Profiles load when the game starts; restart Skyrim after editing one by hand[/*]
[*]Mistakes are reported in [font=Courier New]Romantasy.log[/font], and [font=Courier New]tools/romantasy-profile-check.exe[/font] checks a folder of profiles without starting the game[/*]
[/list]

A profile file owns that follower's personality. Players cannot edit it, and you should not also register the same follower through the older Papyrus registration call.

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Path 2: Dialogue Conditions[/color][/b][/size]

Use the standard [b]GetGraphVariableInt[/b] condition, Run On [b]Subject[/b], with one of these reserved names:

[list]
[*][font=Courier New]Romantasy_Registered[/font] - 1 when Romantasy manages this follower, otherwise 0[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]Romantasy_Level[/font] - the current tier, 1 (Stranger) through 6 (Spouse), or 0 when unmanaged[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]Romantasy_Points[/font] - exact earned points, or -1 when unmanaged[/*]
[/list]

Friend or higher, joined with AND:

[code]GetGraphVariableInt  Romantasy_Registered  == 1
GetGraphVariableInt  Romantasy_Level       >= 3[/code]

Always include the Registered guard, especially with <, <= or != tests. Enter the names without quotation marks. When converting old [font=Courier New]ROM_RomanceLevel[/font] rank checks, add one to the value: the new levels count from 1, the old ranks from 0. Exact point thresholds are unchanged.

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Path 3: The Papyrus Bridge (authored beats)[/color][/b][/size]

To award or remove points at a specific moment (a kiss, a betrayal, a quest beat), call Romantasy from a fragment. Redistribute [font=Courier New]Source\Scripts\Romantasy.psc[/font] with your optional integration source so it compiles against the native bridge. The 2.x functions are unchanged. The API is now capability version 8.

[code]Scriptname Romantasy Hidden

Int Function GetApiVersion() Native Global

Bool Function ModifyPoints(Actor akFollower, Int aiPoints, String asReason = "", Bool abShowLevelUp = True) Native Global
Bool Function ApplyPreference(Actor akFollower, String asStatName, Int aiDelta = 1, Bool abShowLevelUp = True) Native Global

Bool Function ClearPreferences(Actor akFollower) Native Global
Bool Function SetPreference(Actor akFollower, String asStatName, Int aiDirection) Native Global
Int Function GetPreference(Actor akFollower, String asStatName) Native Global
Bool Function SetPreferencesManual(Actor akFollower, Bool abManual = True) Native Global
Bool Function IsPreferencesManual(Actor akFollower) Native Global

Bool Function RegisterAuthorFollower(Actor akFollower, String[] asStatNames, Int[] aiDirections, Int aiStartingLevel = 1, GlobalVariable akRelationshipRankMirror = None) Native Global
Bool Function RegisterAuthorFollowerPointsMirror(Actor akFollower, GlobalVariable akRelationshipPointsMirror) Native Global

Int Function GetPoints(Actor akFollower) Native Global
Int Function GetLevel(Actor akFollower) Native Global
String Function GetLevelName(Actor akFollower) Native Global[/code]

[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]ModifyPoints[/color] - apply an exact authored point change with a reason shown in the recent-changes list[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]ApplyPreference[/color] - apply the follower's configured like or dislike for a statistic; returns False when she has no opinion[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]GetPoints / GetLevel / GetLevelName[/color] - read the current relationship state at any time; GetLevel returns 1 through 6, or 0 when the actor is not managed[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]ClearPreferences / SetPreference / GetPreference[/color] - manage player-created or externally controlled profiles; protected profiles reject writes[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]SetPreferencesManual / IsPreferencesManual[/color] - coordinate ownership with an external profile editor[/*]
[/list]

ModifyPoints and ApplyPreference apply only to a managed follower who is actively following. Example TopicInfo fragment:

[code]Romantasy.ModifyPoints(akSpeaker, 50, "Kissed under the aurora")[/code]

Pass [font=Courier New]abShowLevelUp = False[/font] to apply a change without the tier pop-up or level-change event.

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Path 4: Voiced Reactions via ModEvents[/color][/b][/size]

Romantasy broadcasts two SKSE ModEvents so your follower can speak when the bond moves:

[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Romantasy_OnLevelChanged[/color] - fired when a follower rises into a new tier; [font=Courier New]numArg[/font] is the new level (1 through 6) and [font=Courier New]sender[/font] is her base NPC[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Romantasy_OnPreference[/color] - fired when a tracked activity changes her points without crossing a tier; [font=Courier New]strArg[/font] is the statistic label, [font=Courier New]numArg[/font] is the point change, and [font=Courier New]sender[/font] is her base NPC[/*]
[/list]

The handler signature for both is [font=Courier New](String eventName, String strArg, Float numArg, Form sender)[/font]. Always filter by sender, re-register after loading a save, and consider a cooldown or random chance for frequent preference reactions.

[code]Event OnRomPreference(String eventName, String statLabel, Float delta, Form sender)
    If sender != MyFollowerBase
        Return
    EndIf

    Actor me = GetActorReference()
    If me
        If delta > 0
            me.Say(LikeTopic)
        Else
            me.Say(DislikeTopic)
        EndIf
    EndIf
EndEvent[/code]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Path 5: Older Integrations[/color][/b][/size]

Everything built for 2.x keeps working, and saved points and tiers are untouched:

[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Optional runtime registration[/color] - a compatibility plugin that calls [font=Courier New]RegisterAuthorFollower[/font] (and, from API 6, [font=Courier New]RegisterAuthorFollowerPointsMirror[/font]) from [font=Courier New]OnInit[/font] and [font=Courier New]OnPlayerLoadGame[/font] still works, including the optional rank and points GlobalVariable mirrors[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Faction tags[/color] - followers that master Romantasy and carry [font=Courier New]ROM_RomanceLevel[/font] plus [font=Courier New]ROM_*[/font] preference factions remain supported[/*]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Faction conditions[/color] - [font=Courier New]GetFactionRank ROM_RomanceLevel[/font] (ranks 0 through 5) and the exact-points proxy [font=Courier New]GetFactionRank ROM_RomancePoints[/font] (-1 when unmanaged) keep answering[/*]
[/list]

New releases should prefer a profile file and the GetGraphVariableInt conditions. The included conversion guide walks through moving an existing follower across.


