[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]Compatibility[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#34d399][b]Compatible:[/b][/color]
[list]
[*]The vanilla follower system, Horde, NFF, AFT, EFF, and custom follower frameworks[/*]
[*]Followers supported through a profile file, runtime registration, or the older faction tags[/*]
[*]Followers without author support, added by the player through New Bond[/*]
[*]Custom-voiced followers and follower-specific dialogue, scenes, reactions, quests, and marriage systems[/*]
[*]Other romance and marriage mods; Romantasy maintains its own ledger and does not alter vanilla marriage[/*]
[*]Existing saves; Romantasy can be installed or removed mid-playthrough[/*]
[*]Games and follower names in any language[/*]
[/list]

There are no known follower-framework incompatibilities. A follower who has no author profile and has not been added by the player is simply invisible to Romantasy.

[color=#b8a285][b]Older follower integrations remain supported.[/b] Updating Romantasy does not invalidate their saved scores or relationship tiers.[/color]


[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]Troubleshooting[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#fbbf24][b]My follower does not appear in the dashboard[/b][/color]
If the follower has official Romantasy support, make sure that support is installed and enabled. Otherwise, recruit her normally, bring her with you, open Romantasy, and use New bond. Followers generated at runtime by other mods cannot be added because they have no stable plugin record.

[color=#fbbf24][b]The dashboard does not open[/b][/color]
Confirm that SKSE64 and Address Library match your exact Skyrim runtime and that Magelight UI 1.6 or newer is installed. If Open with Favorites Menu is on, Left Ctrl + R is switched off; cast the Romantasy power instead. Check [font=Courier New]Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/SKSE/Romantasy.log[/font] when reporting a problem.

[color=#fbbf24][b]Names show as question marks[/b][/color]
Update to 3.0.1, which draws letters from other alphabets with Windows' own fonts.

[color=#fbbf24][b]My points did not change after I did something[/b][/color]
The follower may not care about that activity, or she may not have been actively following you when the game recorded it. Tier notifications are also deliberately delayed during combat, although the underlying point change is recorded immediately.

[color=#fbbf24][b]The total changed but Recent Changes looks empty[/b][/color]
Recent Changes belongs to the follower whose dossier is currently selected. Select the same follower whose total changed. The panel keeps the five most recent point changes for that individual bond.

[color=#fbbf24][b]A removed bond came back, or an edit did not stick[/b][/color]
Keep the PlayerProfiles folder (under MO2, usually in Overwrite) when updating or reinstalling. Removing a bond leaves a small disabled profile file on purpose, so an older save cannot bring the bond back.

[color=#fbbf24][b]What happens to Romantasy dialogue when Romantasy is not installed?[/b][/color]
Followers supported through a profile file need nothing from Romantasy in their own plugin. Dialogue guarded by the Registered condition simply does not play, and the follower works as she always did.

[color=#fbbf24][b]Can a follower love and hate the same thing?[/b][/color]
No. Each activity is like, dislike, or neutral for a given follower.

[color=#fbbf24][b]Does this marry my follower in the vanilla system?[/b][/color]
No. The Spouse tier is Romantasy's own bond level. A follower mod can use it as the trigger for a marriage scene, but Romantasy never performs or replaces vanilla marriage.

[color=#fbbf24][b]Will this slow my game down?[/b][/color]
Romantasy's tracker is native SKSE code that reacts to the game's statistic events. The dashboard only draws while it is open, and the Papyrus side is a thin native bridge without update loops.


